WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.110
# Script

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:02.110
## Overview

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:03.110
---

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:04.110
**Hook #1:** Ace, Sabo, and Luffy became brothers
when they shared Sake cups as kids.

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:05.110
And in that moment they dreamed about one
day being incredible pirates.

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:06.110
So what if instead of going their separate
ways, they all managed to set out to sea together.

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:07.110
How would their journey go?

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:08.110
And would Luffy still follow his dream to
become pirate king?

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:09.110
In other words, what would happen if Ace,
Sabo, and Luffy formed a pirate crew?

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:10.110
**Hook #2:** Sabo was nearly killed at ten
years old.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.110
Ace left when he was seventeen.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.110
And Luffy started his own pirate adventure
three years later, which left these three

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:13.110
adopted brothers separated until much later
in the story.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:17.610
But what if these three ridiculously strong
kids had somehow stuck together and formed

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.221
one of the most exciting pirate crews ever.

00:00:20.221 --> 00:00:21.221
In other words, what would have happened if
Ace, Sabo, and Luffy formed a pirate crew

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:22.221
together?

00:00:22.221 --> 00:00:23.221
**Hook #3:** Have you ever wondered how Ace,
Sabo, and Luffy would do as a pirate crew?

00:00:23.221 --> 00:00:24.221
Would they sweep through the grand line and
find the One Piece easily?

00:00:24.221 --> 00:00:25.221
Or would they be crushed as the cocky kids
that they are?

00:00:25.221 --> 00:00:26.221
Let’s find out what would happen if Ace,
Sabo, and Luffy formed a pirate crew.

00:00:26.221 --> 00:00:27.221
**Script - 4200 Words without intro**

00:00:27.221 --> 00:00:28.221
**Hook goes here.**

00:00:28.221 --> 00:00:29.221
Sabo was nearly killed at ten years old.

00:00:29.221 --> 00:00:30.221
Ace left when he was seventeen.

00:00:30.221 --> 00:00:31.221
And Luffy started his own pirate adventure
three years later, which left these three

00:00:31.221 --> 00:00:32.221
adopted brothers separated until much later
in the story.

00:00:32.221 --> 00:00:33.221
But what if these three ridiculously strong
kids had somehow stuck together and formed

00:00:33.221 --> 00:00:34.221
one of the most exciting pirate crews ever.

00:00:34.221 --> 00:00:35.221
In other words, what would have happened if
Ace, Sabo, and Luffy formed a pirate crew?

00:00:35.221 --> 00:00:36.221
Well, of course everything would begin back
in the Goa Kingdom, where Ace, Sabo, and Luffy

00:00:36.221 --> 00:00:37.221
all grew up together.

00:00:37.221 --> 00:00:38.221
And our version of the story kicks of the
moment when the royals of the island are about

00:00:38.221 --> 00:00:42.430
to burn this massive heap of trash to get
rid of all of the poor people to not leave

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:47.930
a bad impression on the celestial dragons
who were coming to visit.

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:53.420
You might remember that this is where Ace
and Luffy were nearly killed by these thugs

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:57.510
[Show Bluejam pirates ch 587], and after this
event, Sabo was so disgusted by his wealthy

00:00:57.510 --> 00:01:01.390
family that he just wanted to get out of there
[ch 587].

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:08.439
Now originally he set out in a little boat
and got absolutely destroyed by this celestial

00:01:08.439 --> 00:01:12.800
dragon ship [ch 585], but for our scenario,
let’s imagine that Luffy and Ace somehow

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.970
manage to stop Sabo from leaving the island.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:20.820
Maybe they kidnap him from his parents and
fake his death or even intercept him before

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:22.700
he is about to set sail.

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:27.860
And now they continue their lives as they
had since Luffy joined.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:33.290
They live up in the mountains, training and
growing stronger until the day they are ready

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:35.259
to begin their pirate journey.

00:01:35.259 --> 00:01:37.700
And that day comes seven years later.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:42.700
Ace and Sabo are now seventeen, while Luffy
is still only fourteen.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:47.200
So yes, Luffy is going to set out WAY SOONER
than he did in the original story.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:52.040
And while you might say he MUST ABSOLUTELY
wait until he is seventeen, I just don’t

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:55.970
see Ace and Sabo waiting around until they
are twenty to head out to sea.

00:01:55.970 --> 00:02:00.240
So in order for these three to stay together,
they have to leave now.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:05.140
This leads them to buy a ship with all the
treasure they’ve stolen, and finally set

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:06.770
out into the ocean.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:12.860
Which seeing how Luffy almost drowned when
he first started [ch 2], this could quickly

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.550
end in disaster.

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:19.020
But thankfully Sabo always had an interest
in navigation [ch 585], which helps them to

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:22.560
at least survive one day at sea.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:27.200
But hold on tight because there are major
problems coming up very soon.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:33.019
But the first big question is… where do
they go from here?

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:35.200
Luffy wants to go somewhere to get some food.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.340
Sabo wants to head to a nearby island.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:42.020
And Ace wants to track down this mysterious
bounty hunter he has heard so much about [hint

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:43.020
at zoro].

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:46.150
But with all three pulling the sails in different
directions [show each of them pulling on a

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:50.750
rope in a different direction, they snap the
mast, and their ship is hopelessly broken.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:53.890
Well, that lasted only a short time.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:58.600
Now the three drift helplessly until they
crash land on this mysterious island [Show

00:02:58.600 --> 00:02:59.620
Sixis island from Ace novel].

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:03.950
But before we see the game-changing events
on this island, let’s shift back to when

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:09.860
these three were kids, because back in ch
585 there is a super important moment here

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:14.150
that we MUST understand to see how this crew
will turn out in the future.

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:19.360
[All of this up next is in ch 585] Here they
basically explain what each of their dreams

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:20.360
are.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:22.830
Sabo just wants to be free from the oppression
of his parents.

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:27.409
On the other hand, Ace simply wants people
to know his name and recognize him for who

00:03:27.409 --> 00:03:28.409
he is.

00:03:28.409 --> 00:03:32.720
Remember he is still dealing with the shame
and guilt of being the son of the former pirate

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:33.720
king.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:38.330
And Luffy shares his own secret dream – no,
not becoming the king of the pirates, but

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:43.260
the one we are still waiting to learn in the
current story.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:45.370
Probably to throw a giant party or something.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:50.530
However, Ace and Sabo think it is hilarious,
but then we get to their first real point

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:57.310
of conflict and one of the reasons they never
made a crew in the first place.

00:03:57.310 --> 00:04:02.770
They all basically assumed that they would
be the captain of their own ship and the others

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:04.470
would join their crew.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:09.299
But none of the others obviously wanted that,
so they originally decided to meet up again

00:04:09.299 --> 00:04:11.650
once they were all strong pirates.

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:16.130
So fast forward again to their current situation,
and the three are shipwrecked on this island

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:22.330
– which by the way is from the Ace novel
– and they meet this crusty fellow Masked

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:23.330
Deuce.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:28.650
Now, Deuce was also shipwrecked here, and
they are basically stuck and starving until

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:34.370
Ace finds this random mysterious fruit [show
Mero Mero no mi].

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:39.610
A hungry Deuce nearly kills Ace to get the
fruit, but after Ace takes the first bite,

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:43.770
he shares the rest with everyone else.

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:48.099
This of course gives Ace his fire powers,
so that part is unchanged from the story.

00:04:48.099 --> 00:04:52.130
And with his new abilities, they are able
to make a decent raft to help them get off

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:57.360
the island and Deuce of course comes along
as the first new member of the crew.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:03.190
And he’s not just some random guy, he actually
comes from a medical family, so he can serve

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:05.100
as the crew’s doctor.

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:07.310
But wait, aren’t we forgetting something?

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:14.251
A new crew needs a name, so at this point
they decide to call themselves the Sake Cup

00:05:14.251 --> 00:05:18.210
pirates, based on the sake cups that represent
their bond.

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:22.020
Now, their four member crew is going to need
a new ship.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:27.090
So whatever island they find next, they manage
to steal a boat and continue on their journey.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:31.880
But instead of heading straight for the grand
line, they decide to actually be smart for

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:37.550
once and spend some time gaining experience
in the East Blue.

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:43.870
They still don’t have an official captain
yet, but they decide on a system of voting

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:45.270
on where to go next.

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:51.430
And this leads them to travel around, defeating
other pirate crews and making a name for themselves.

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:57.490
And while Luffy himself is younger and weaker
than when he first set out, this is more than

00:05:57.490 --> 00:06:00.970
made up for by having the powerful Ace and
Sabo along.

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:06.400
Plus, they spent all those years continuing
to train together, so I think this version

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:11.570
of Luffy might even be stronger than he normally
was at 14.

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:13.470
So during these roughly six months.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:16.449
They meet and recruit Usopp.

00:06:16.449 --> 00:06:20.500
Now, Usopp is also younger, but he is still
an orphan.

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:24.970
The whole conflict on his island isn’t even
happening yet, so there is no one to defeat

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:30.560
here, but Usopp and Luffy get along so well
that Luffy invites him to join and Usopp accepts.

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:38.699
However, they don’t get the Merry since
they never actually saved the village.

00:06:38.699 --> 00:06:42.130
There’s a similar circumstance with Sanji.

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:47.039
After the Sake Cup pirates come to this floating
restaurant [Baratie] to recruit a cook, let’s

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:50.830
just say they somehow convince Sanji to join
them as well.

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:56.660
Maybe Zeff kicks him out or he decides to
follow his dream to find the All Blue.

00:06:56.660 --> 00:07:00.060
However, Nami joining is a bit more of an
issue.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:05.110
Because remember that Nami only originally
joined Luffy to steal his money.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:09.970
Then after he rescued her village she actually
became part of the crew.

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:14.020
But in this version of the story, the Sake
Cup pirates probably wouldn’t encounter

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:19.150
this clown pirate [Buggy] yet because he would
not have invaded Orange Town until years later.

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:21.970
So that means no initial encounter with Nami.

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:27.300
However, I definitely think the Sake Cup pirates
would eventually come to Nami’s island.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:31.790
And while Ace would probably not want to get
involved with the fishmen, Sabo and Luffy

00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:35.870
would never stand for the people of the island
being enslaved to Arlong.

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:42.240
So together, the three beat down the notorious
fishman, and save the people of the village.

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:44.710
This leads Nami to officially join the crew.

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:50.360
And while Sabo is also a navigator, Nami is
literally going to be the greatest navigator

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:54.310
in the world, so he can take a back seat to
our orange haired navigating-goddess.

00:07:54.310 --> 00:08:00.660
So Usopp, Sanji, Nami, and, wait… aren’t
we missing someone?

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:05.470
Now remember that we are now about two and
half years before the start of the original

00:08:05.470 --> 00:08:11.730
story, Zoro would not have been captured at
Shell Town and would still be out bounty hunting.

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:17.720
Which means it is highly likely that the green-haired
swordsman would cross paths with the Sake

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:18.720
Cup pirates.

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:24.060
And I think that they would actually develop
a respectful rivalry over these months, where

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:28.210
Zoro keeps coming after them, but is beaten
down each time by one of the brothers.

00:08:28.210 --> 00:08:33.620
And then at the last moment before the Sake
Cup pirates head to the grand line, he tries

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:35.340
to beat them one last time.

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:41.860
Of course he would fail, but the crew would
then invite him to join them on their adventure,

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:43.599
and he would of course agree.

00:08:43.599 --> 00:08:44.599
So bam!

00:08:44.599 --> 00:08:51.959
The gang’s all here, with a few extras,
and let’s continue forward, to all of the

00:08:51.959 --> 00:08:58.149
unbelievable changes that are coming in the
Grand Line and the mind-blowing future that

00:08:58.149 --> 00:09:00.890
awaits this incredible young crew.

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:05.149
Now again, Luffy and the other original straw
hats are all still about two and a half years

00:09:05.149 --> 00:09:10.660
younger than they were before, but that also
means events cannot play out just like they

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:12.720
did in the original story.

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:17.940
This won’t be the speedrun version of the
Grand Line like in the original story, as

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:23.360
the crew will take more time going from island
to island.

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:26.279
However, things are going to be much different.

00:09:26.279 --> 00:09:31.430
For example, Alabasta would not be having
its civil war, so we will basically skip that

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:32.430
whole arc.

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:34.680
Which means no Robin, for now.

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:39.830
And since Masked Deuce is the crew’s doctor,
the crew don’t go looking for another one,

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:42.079
so we miss Chopper as well.

00:09:42.079 --> 00:09:46.610
Before we go any further, there is one super
important thing we haven’t yet discussed

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:49.870
in the power dynamics of the crew.

00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:55.779
After six months in the East Blue, Sabo, Ace,
and Luffy have all gotten much stronger.

00:09:55.779 --> 00:10:01.410
And especially Ace with his logia powers can
easily take on nearly anyone they meet in

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:03.079
this part of the world.

00:10:03.079 --> 00:10:11.990
And for now, Luffy is still the weakest of
the three brothers, but that gap is rapidly

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:12.990
closing.

00:10:12.990 --> 00:10:17.550
And at this point, the crew would still want
to go to Skypiea, so that whole arc continues

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:19.700
pretty normally.

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:24.440
The lightning fruit user Enel is already oppressing
the Skpieans.

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:28.959
And while the others aren’t too sure about
getting involved, Luffy absolutely refuses

00:10:28.959 --> 00:10:31.910
to leave without freeing the people from the
false god.

00:10:31.910 --> 00:10:35.930
The rest of the crew supports his decision,
and so they start the battle.

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:40.360
Luffy and Ace can certainly fight him with
their Rubber and Logia powers, and I think

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:46.010
Sabo is smart enough to find some seastone
to be able to contribute to the fight and

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:51.279
eventually take down the lightning man, which
would also basically ruin his plans to get

00:10:51.279 --> 00:10:55.620
to the moon, since his ark Maxim [ch 278]
was not yet completed.

00:10:55.620 --> 00:11:00.220
Although they wouldn’t be able to read the
poneglyph next to the golden bell since Robin

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:02.130
is not with them at this time.

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:06.760
Now with this country freed, and after they
have a massive party, the crew can continue

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:10.740
back down to the ocean, with one major change
in the crew’s structure.

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:17.470
By now, I think the crew would be ready to
accept Luffy as the captain.

00:11:17.470 --> 00:11:22.070
He is the most headstrong and determined to
help others.

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:27.050
Plus both Ace and Sabo eventually joined other
crews – those being the Emperor Whitebeard

00:11:27.050 --> 00:11:31.899
for Ace and the Revolutionary Army for Sabo
– so I don’t think it is that much of

00:11:31.899 --> 00:11:36.480
a stretch to think they would eventually be
okay with Luffy being the captain.

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:43.079
Plus Luffy’s dream to become pirate king
is the goal that unites everyone elses’.

00:11:43.079 --> 00:11:47.370
Ace already has made a name for himself and
has people who love him.

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:53.400
Sabo is free and helps free oppressed countries,
so really Luffy is the one driving everyone

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:54.400
forward.

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:59.220
And this doesn’t mean that Luffy will make
every single choice, because he doesn’t

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:02.680
even do that with the straw hats.

00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:06.960
This is a super important decision that will
be tested right away because after the rigorous

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:12.200
journey to reach the sky islands, the Sake
Cup crew’s ship is in very bad shape.

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:16.089
Now remember that this is not the Merry, since
they did not get her from Usopp’s hometown,

00:12:16.089 --> 00:12:21.000
but the crew would no doubt have some attachment
to the ship.

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:25.830
This could be a case where the crew might
be split on buying a new ship or repairing

00:12:25.830 --> 00:12:30.120
their current one, but just like in the original
story, Luffy would probably see the need to

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:31.410
buy a new ship.

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:36.870
But we wouldn’t get the whole Usopp leaving
drama since he isn’t as attached to this

00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:37.870
ship.

00:12:37.870 --> 00:12:41.449
So with a new ship, and probably a new shipwright
crewmate [show Paulie from Galley La], the

00:12:41.449 --> 00:12:43.480
crew depart for Sabaody.

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:44.500
Wait, what?

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:46.079
What about Franky?

00:12:46.079 --> 00:12:47.110
What about Enies Lobby?

00:12:47.110 --> 00:12:52.270
Well, at this point the crew doesn’t have
Robin, so there would be no way for these

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:54.930
government secret agents [end of ch 345] to
blackmail them.

00:12:54.930 --> 00:13:00.510
And that whole saga was the reason the crew
befriended Franky, so if none of that happened

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:05.329
then they wouldn’t be able to have Franky
build the Thousand Sunny OR recruit him to

00:13:05.329 --> 00:13:06.329
the crew.

00:13:06.329 --> 00:13:11.150
But they would need a shipwright, so maybe
they recruit this guy [Paulie], who is constantly

00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:13.160
running from gambling debt.

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:17.530
So wow this is shaping up to be a pretty incredible
crew.

00:13:17.530 --> 00:13:20.130
But you want to know the saddest thing about
this group.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:25.290
No Franky means we will never have the straw
hats strongest combo attack, the pirates docking

00:13:25.290 --> 00:13:26.290
six [ch 472].

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:31.870
But you can still use your most overpowered
combo attack to mash that subscribe button.

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:36.889
Even without Franky though, there’s much
more insane things to come for this headstrong

00:13:36.889 --> 00:13:37.889
crew.

00:13:37.889 --> 00:13:43.029
They continue to sail around, before eventually
getting sucked into the zombie-infested Thriller

00:13:43.029 --> 00:13:47.620
Bark, where they still meet and recruit Brook
because Luffy has always wanted a musician.

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:54.190
So no major changes here, and after curb-stomping
the shadow man the group sail to Sabaody.

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:58.880
And here is where we are going to dive into
the truly game-changing alterations to the

00:13:58.880 --> 00:13:59.880
story.

00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:04.759
Because in Sabaody everything is going to
go… *pause for dramatic tension* smoothly.

00:14:04.759 --> 00:14:05.759
That’s right.

00:14:05.759 --> 00:14:09.899
The craziest part is that nothing crazy happens.

00:14:09.899 --> 00:14:13.330
They could still somehow meet this mermaid
[Camie ch 490] and this fishman [Hatchan ch

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:16.880
496] who takes them to meet the former right
hand of the pirate king, Silvers Rayleigh.

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:21.550
And Rayleigh is super excited to meet them
all after learning about them from Shanks,

00:14:21.550 --> 00:14:26.300
and he immediately agrees to coat their ship
so they can travel under the Grand Line.

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:30.589
And with his two older brothers watching over
him, Luffy stays out of trouble.

00:14:30.589 --> 00:14:35.019
In fact, Rayleigh even gives the crew a hardcore
crash course training camp, which we’ll

00:14:35.019 --> 00:14:37.009
talk more about in just a moment.

00:14:37.009 --> 00:14:41.610
Then after a few days they dive underwater
towards fishman island.

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:44.470
So, if you’re following along, that means
NO.

00:14:44.470 --> 00:14:45.470
TWO.

00:14:45.470 --> 00:14:46.470
YEAR.

00:14:46.470 --> 00:14:47.470
TIMESKIP.

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:53.089
Which is a HUGE CHANGE that is going to have
massive consequences for the next part of

00:14:53.089 --> 00:14:54.089
the story.

00:14:54.089 --> 00:14:56.880
Of course this means that we are skipping
all of the Summit War Saga.

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:00.279
So no Amazon Lily, Impel Down, or even Marineford.

00:15:00.279 --> 00:15:05.060
Because this time the donut man [Ace donut]
is safe and sound.

00:15:05.060 --> 00:15:08.699
Which makes this the perfect time to talk
about the world government.

00:15:08.699 --> 00:15:12.899
Because at this time, the Sake Cup pirates
are pretty famous.

00:15:12.899 --> 00:15:19.399
Luffy, Ace, Sabo, and even Zoro might all
be part of the worst generation of upcoming

00:15:19.399 --> 00:15:24.210
pirates, but the world government would not
care about them nearly as much as they hated

00:15:24.210 --> 00:15:26.430
the straw hats.

00:15:26.430 --> 00:15:28.120
Because there was no fiasco in Alabasta.

00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:30.470
No shooting down the flag in Enies Lobby.

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:37.589
No stealing Robin from CP9, so to the world
government, this is just another group of

00:15:37.589 --> 00:15:42.819
annoying pirates, although they would probably
still be keeping an eye on Luffy and Ace because

00:15:42.819 --> 00:15:44.210
of their lineage.

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:47.930
And since there’s no Marineford that means
Luffy didn’t spend all that time training

00:15:47.930 --> 00:15:49.029
during the timeskip.

00:15:49.029 --> 00:15:53.420
However, as I just mentioned, they did get
a crash course training with Rayleigh before

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:59.510
they left fishman island, where the dark king
at least showed them the basic idea of haki.

00:15:59.510 --> 00:16:04.990
And characters like Sabo and Zoro, who don’t
have devil fruits, will be especially excited

00:16:04.990 --> 00:16:10.220
to learn haki so that they can continue to
be able to fight strong devil fruit users.

00:16:10.220 --> 00:16:14.120
Now at this point, the Sake Cup pirates are
a pretty fearsome group.

00:16:14.120 --> 00:16:19.350
They sail through fishman island and the early
parts of the new world without much trouble.

00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:25.440
But everything changes when they encounter
the Whitebeard pirates on some random island.

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:30.880
Which is a mind-blowing event for this crew,
because up until now, they have never faced

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:34.760
off against any of the top tier fighters in
the world.

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:39.130
Of course the Sake Cup pirates get beaten
down by the Emperor’s crew.

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:43.779
Now I can imagine that just like in the original
story, Whitebeard might invite the Sake Cup

00:16:43.779 --> 00:16:45.279
pirates to join his crew.

00:16:45.279 --> 00:16:50.750
And while Ace originally accepted his offer,
I don’t think Luffy would ever agree to

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:56.130
work under anyone else, so Whitebeard could
either kill them here, or the more likely

00:16:56.130 --> 00:17:00.509
case is I think he would let them go because
he sees something special in Luffy and the

00:17:00.509 --> 00:17:01.509
crew.

00:17:01.509 --> 00:17:06.510
Which is a super lucky break, because not
everyone survives an encounter with an Emperor’s

00:17:06.510 --> 00:17:07.510
crew.

00:17:07.510 --> 00:17:09.760
So time passes as they sail around the New
World.

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:15.910
They are exploring new islands, fighting strong
opponents, and growing stronger.

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:20.510
Luffy would probably have mastered at least
Gear 2 and 3.

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:23.220
Maybe even 4 if he practiced his haki enough.

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:28.120
And at this point over a year has passed in
the new world, and we are roughly a year behind

00:17:28.120 --> 00:17:29.700
the original story.

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:35.559
Eventually, we come to one of the most dangerous
islands in the New World: Wano.

00:17:35.559 --> 00:17:40.370
Where the Sake Cup pirates are in for their
next rude awakening.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:45.210
As they travel up the waterfall, the crew
gets separated just like in the original story

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:46.210
[ch 910].

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:50.540
Now remember we are too early in the timeline
for this to play out like the normal Wano.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:55.340
The samurai who were sent forward in time
have not yet arrived, but the country is still

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:57.350
being dominated by Kaido.

00:17:57.350 --> 00:18:02.299
And Luffy being Luffy, he would of course
want to save the oppressed people.

00:18:02.299 --> 00:18:08.710
And Luffy on his own eventually leads to a
major smackdown by Kaido [ch 923] and Luffy

00:18:08.710 --> 00:18:11.150
is thrown in jail [ch 924].

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:14.920
At this same time, Sabo, Ace, and the rest
of the crew have come to Onigashima looking

00:18:14.920 --> 00:18:15.920
for Luffy.

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:19.330
They encounter Kaido’s child, Yamato [ch
984], and after quickly becoming friends,

00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:21.344
they find the key to her handcuffs and break
her free.

00:18:21.344 --> 00:18:25.190
Yamato would of course want to join the crew,
and together the crew heads off to save Luffy

00:18:25.190 --> 00:18:26.450
from the prison.

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:32.040
And we can argue about the battle here and
the crew defeating this funky dinosaur [Queen],

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:38.370
but eventually the crew save Luffy, as well
as this samurai fishman, Kawamatsu [ch 948].

00:18:38.370 --> 00:18:48.670
Luffy is all fired up to make another attempt
at the boss [Kaido] ,but Kawamatsu, who was

00:18:48.670 --> 00:18:53.450
one of the legendary samurai Oden’s retainers,
tells them that the time to free Wano has

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:55.760
not yet arrived.

00:18:55.760 --> 00:19:01.059
He asks them to come back in one year to help
liberate Wano from Kaido’s tyrannical rule.

00:19:01.059 --> 00:19:09.909
Despite Luffy wanting to help now, the crew
departs, and now things become super interesting,

00:19:09.909 --> 00:19:14.039
because with Yamato on board, we have a top
tier fighter on the crew who can even teach

00:19:14.039 --> 00:19:17.390
them about conquerors and advanced forms of
haki.

00:19:17.390 --> 00:19:20.640
Which brings us to a super important stretch
of the story.

00:19:20.640 --> 00:19:25.080
Because we skipped over much of the normal
new world islands, but I think one arc that

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:29.700
was incredibly important is the home of the
minks Zou.

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:35.460
Kawamatsu should know about Zou since the
Kozuki and Minks are allies, so before separating,

00:19:35.460 --> 00:19:40.990
Kawamatsu gives them a vivre card that will
help them find the massive elephant Zunesha.

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:46.049
This leads the Sake Cup pirates to climb up
the elephant, where they make friends with

00:19:46.049 --> 00:19:47.380
the animal Minks.

00:19:47.380 --> 00:19:52.720
But the major question is do the minks show
Luffy and the crew the poneglyphs.

00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:57.429
You could argue that they would not, since
there is no one from the Kozuki clan with

00:19:57.429 --> 00:19:58.429
the crew.

00:19:58.429 --> 00:20:01.570
Plus they wouldn’t have just saved the entire
tribe.

00:20:01.570 --> 00:20:05.440
But maybe they have a letter from Kawamatsu
who tells the mink leaders to show them the

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:06.440
poneglyphs.

00:20:06.440 --> 00:20:11.380
But even if they do get to see the Road poneglyph
and learn all about the secret stones, they

00:20:11.380 --> 00:20:15.670
definitely can’t read it yet.

00:20:15.670 --> 00:20:21.520
Still, it is one step closer to Luffy’s
dream of becoming pirate king.

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:25.660
They could even take on a new crewmate, like
Pedro, who wanted to serve the pirate king,

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:29.659
or Carrot might sneak aboard even if she wasn’t
invited.

00:20:29.659 --> 00:20:33.700
After Zou, they continue sailing through the
New World and practicing the advanced forms

00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:34.700
of haki.

00:20:34.700 --> 00:20:39.170
At this point I would say Luffy, Sabo, and
Ace and probably even Zoro are definitely

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:43.880
above Warlord power level, so they can pretty
easily defeat people like the sand fruit user

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:49.620
Crocodile and the string fruit user Doflamingo,
which will be important in just a few moments.

00:20:49.620 --> 00:20:54.549
However, they are still undermatched against
the Yonko, and when they next encounter Whitebeard,

00:20:54.549 --> 00:20:58.000
they are once again defeated by the world’s
strongest man and his crew.

00:20:58.000 --> 00:21:02.789
Though at this point, Whitebeard is getting
older and sick, and the battle is much closer

00:21:02.789 --> 00:21:05.179
than it was the first time around.

00:21:05.179 --> 00:21:10.169
With Whitebeard impressed by how much the
Sake Cup crew has grown, I think they would

00:21:10.169 --> 00:21:14.260
probably become allies and could even exchange
vivre cards.

00:21:14.260 --> 00:21:19.230
Around this time they could also find Elbaf
where Shanks could be waiting, but I still

00:21:19.230 --> 00:21:24.450
don’t think Shanks would be ready to acknowledge
Luffy yet, so they might just skip this island

00:21:24.450 --> 00:21:25.450
for now.

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:29.230
But one island they would definitely go to
is Roadstar Island.

00:21:29.230 --> 00:21:35.120
In case you forgot, Roadstar is the last island
of the Grand Line, and it is originally where

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:38.070
pirates are supposed to learn about the poneglyphs.

00:21:38.070 --> 00:21:42.090
And even though the Sake Cup pirates might
have already learned about them from Zou,

00:21:42.090 --> 00:21:46.680
this would be a good place to stop because
it would help them learn more about the mysterious

00:21:46.680 --> 00:21:47.680
stones.

00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:51.690
Although Luffy does have the voice of all
things, it is not quite the same as someone

00:21:51.690 --> 00:21:53.570
who can literally read them.

00:21:53.570 --> 00:22:01.150
And this actually sets them on a path to sail
the grand line again to find the poneglyphs,

00:22:01.150 --> 00:22:03.529
just like Roger did.

00:22:03.529 --> 00:22:09.790
Although Ace might not like that they are
following in his father’s footsteps.

00:22:09.790 --> 00:22:14.650
Regardless, this now overpowered crew goes
all the way back to Reverse mountain and starts

00:22:14.650 --> 00:22:15.890
the journey again.

00:22:15.890 --> 00:22:19.870
And this time they liberate the islands they
skipped in the past.

00:22:19.870 --> 00:22:24.080
For example,&nbsp; Crocodile would have already
taken control of Alabasta and the civil war

00:22:24.080 --> 00:22:29.760
might already be over, but Luffy, Ace, and
Sabo could come in and take down the Warlord.

00:22:29.760 --> 00:22:35.429
This would also be the perfect time for Robin
to join the crew, which means that CP9 could

00:22:35.429 --> 00:22:37.390
also try to blackmail her again.

00:22:37.390 --> 00:22:42.309
But this might be a good thing, because the
crew would have no trouble smacking down these

00:22:42.309 --> 00:22:44.570
secret agents [show lucci, kaku, kalifa, etc…].

00:22:44.570 --> 00:22:49.320
Ahh, it feels good to see the crew dealing
some punishment after they took such a beating

00:22:49.320 --> 00:22:50.760
in the original story.

00:22:50.760 --> 00:22:56.610
But with Robin back on board, and fully trusting
the crew, they return to the New World, saving

00:22:56.610 --> 00:22:58.600
islands and finding poneglyphs.

00:22:58.600 --> 00:23:02.360
This would be how the journey continues for
a while.

00:23:02.360 --> 00:23:05.560
The crew might even establish a home base
island somewhere.

00:23:05.560 --> 00:23:10.929
But then something happens that shakes the
entire pirate world.

00:23:10.929 --> 00:23:15.909
Blackbeard betrays Whitebeard and steals his
darkness Logia fruit.

00:23:15.909 --> 00:23:22.299
And this single event is going to set off
a crazy chain reaction that massively affect

00:23:22.299 --> 00:23:23.690
the story.

00:23:23.690 --> 00:23:25.309
Blackbeard could still become a warlord.

00:23:25.309 --> 00:23:31.059
He could still break into Impel Down and gather
a stupidly powerful crew and go around collecting

00:23:31.059 --> 00:23:32.590
devil fruits.

00:23:32.590 --> 00:23:37.010
Then he could eventually return to challenge
Whitebeard in a straight up fight.

00:23:37.010 --> 00:23:41.559
Which is actually not Blackbeard’s style,
but with Whitebeard sick and already dying,

00:23:41.559 --> 00:23:48.279
I think Blackbeard would certainly kill Whitebeard
and take his legendary devil fruit.

00:23:48.279 --> 00:23:52.120
However, remember that at this point, the
Sake Cup Crew and Whitebeard’s crew were

00:23:52.120 --> 00:23:53.360
basically allies.

00:23:53.360 --> 00:23:58.150
And when the crew notices Whitebeard’s vivre
card disintegrating, they would do everything

00:23:58.150 --> 00:24:00.150
in their power to save him.

00:24:00.150 --> 00:24:06.690
However, they would likely be too late, but
this would definitely set up the fated showdown

00:24:06.690 --> 00:24:08.920
between Blackbeard and Luffy.

00:24:08.920 --> 00:24:13.470
Now there are many ways this battle could
go.

00:24:13.470 --> 00:24:18.260
Blackbeard is so sneaky that he could trick
Luffy somehow and defeat the crew.

00:24:18.260 --> 00:24:24.580
But the Sake Cup pirates are so insanely powerful
at this point that it might not matter.

00:24:24.580 --> 00:24:28.360
Sabo and Ace would be nearly as strong as
Luffy.

00:24:28.360 --> 00:24:34.179
Plus with Yamato, Zoro, and Sanji, there’s
just no way they could all lose to the darkness

00:24:34.179 --> 00:24:37.260
Logia user who barely got his second fruit.

00:24:37.260 --> 00:24:44.190
However, I do think it would be fitting that
during this battle Luffy finally awakens his

00:24:44.190 --> 00:24:46.450
mythical Sun God Nika fruit.

00:24:46.450 --> 00:24:50.830
This would undoubtedly help him defeat Blackbeard,
and together with his brothers, they would

00:24:50.830 --> 00:24:52.679
avenge Whitebeard’s death.

00:24:52.679 --> 00:24:59.779
Which means that after this battle, the Sake
Cup crew would be on a whole other level.

00:24:59.779 --> 00:25:02.250
Luffy would surely become an Emperor.

00:25:02.250 --> 00:25:07.840
And the only thing stopping them from finding
the One piece would be the last few Road Poneglyphs.

00:25:07.840 --> 00:25:13.580
However, one opponent we haven’t really
mentioned that much is the World Government.

00:25:13.580 --> 00:25:14.580
At this point Luffy’s bounty would have
to be absurdly high.

00:25:14.580 --> 00:25:18.260
In fact, they might see Luffy as so much of
a threat after awakening his devil fruit that

00:25:18.260 --> 00:25:23.450
they slap him with a bounty way way higher
than anything the world has ever seen.

00:25:23.450 --> 00:25:27.840
Their goal would probably be to make Luffy
the number one target of every marine, bounty

00:25:27.840 --> 00:25:33.070
hunter, and pirate in the New World, which
is an absolutely insane target to have on

00:25:33.070 --> 00:25:34.070
your back.

00:25:34.070 --> 00:25:40.419
In fact, turning it up to 11, I figured out
exactly how having an insane one hundred billion

00:25:40.419 --> 00:25:45.630
berry bounty would change Luffy's journey,
and you can watch that right here.

00:25:45.630 --> 00:25:48.780
Shanks for watching, and I’ll see you in
the next one.

